Problem - best time to buy and sell stock

so Brute Force approach for this problem is by using nested for loop
public int maxProfitBruteForce(int[] prices) {
    int maxProfit = 0;
    int n = prices.length;
    
    // Outer loop loops through the buying days
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        // Inner loop loops through the future selling days
        for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
            int profit = prices[j] - prices[i];
            if (profit > maxProfit) {
                maxProfit = profit;
            }
        }
    }
    return maxProfit;
}

So in this we substract the each value of j with i and store it in profit variable 
and compare it with maxProfit if it is greater than we assigned it to the maxProfit 
but why we do this . Because the problem asks the maximum profit so we find that window and returns only the maximum.


